### Match commands -> POST /matches/{matchId}/events
### Set matchId from the CreateMatch.http response, then run blocks top-down.
### Every MatchCommand is wired in MatchService.handle: lifecycle, scoring,
### discipline, penalties, VAR and added time. Success is 202 Accepted.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@matchId = defb824d-7536-41ef-82fc-655189cfaef1

### Clubs and players below are the real rows seeded by players_seed.sql.
### Home: Esperance. Away: Sfaxien.
@esperance = 0dffeae0-bb2e-4608-9e19-aa635e70adfc
@sfaxien = 7354f9c8-7885-4705-9fd0-e26fa6fa7997

### Esperance players
@boualia = 2de218fd-e3e1-4614-937f-ff925a41f0ef
@meriah = 46e3d23f-44c2-4803-b845-0a2d888e74a5
@rafia = 2a756aed-0440-4847-9075-6f9d04a21fd0
@msakni = eaf770b7-8060-4b9f-8ab8-2af6edd5f35f
@belaili = 75c55e8e-7184-40b9-a79c-bccd5ca56653

### Sfaxien players
@omarBenAli = 02c8a2c6-a150-4449-b711-0ba24a73d447
@maaloul = 2d2ee346-5b1d-430b-9f23-9dcba8392cc1
@belwafi = 66549573-e83e-4af3-8caf-2edac7757d0a
@onana = d8e85a30-f2eb-474a-9b72-bffb742f708f

### A UUID that is in no players row at all.
@ghostPlayer = deadbeef-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### A real club that is not in this match. Only Esperance and Sfaxien are
### seeded, so create one through CreateClub.http and paste its id here
### before running block 46.
@thirdClub = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### HAPPY PATH: SCHEDULED -> IN_PROGRESS -> HALF_TIME -> IN_PROGRESS -> COMPLETED
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1. Kick off. Expects 202. Status SCHEDULED -> IN_PROGRESS, scores set to 0-0.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "MATCH_STARTED"
}

### 2. Half-time whistle. Expects 202. IN_PROGRESS -> HALF_TIME.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "FIRST_HALF_ENDED"
}

### 3. Second half kick off. Expects 202. HALF_TIME -> IN_PROGRESS.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "SECOND_HALF_STARTED"
}

### 4. Full time. Expects 202. IN_PROGRESS -> COMPLETED.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "FULL_TIME"
}

### 5. Verify the projection reflects the replayed events.
GET {{host}}/matches

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### ALTERNATE ENDINGS (use a fresh matchId for each)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 6. Postpone a match that never started. SCHEDULED -> POSTPONED.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "MATCH_POSTPONED",
  "reason": "Waterlogged pitch"
}

### 7. Abandon a match already in progress. IN_PROGRESS -> ABANDONED.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "MATCH_ABANDONED",
  "reason": "Floodlight failure",
  "minute": 63
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### GUARD RAILS: every one of these must be rejected by the aggregate
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 8. Start a match twice. Second call expects failure: "Match must be in scheduled state".
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "MATCH_STARTED"
}

### 9. Second half without a half-time first. Expects "match is not in half time".
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "SECOND_HALF_STARTED"
}

### 10. Half-time whistle while at HALF_TIME. Expects "match is not in progress".
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "FIRST_HALF_ENDED"
}

### 11. Full time on a COMPLETED / SCHEDULED match. Expects "match is not in progress".
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "FULL_TIME"
}

### 12. Postpone a match that already kicked off. Expects "match must be scheduled".
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "MATCH_POSTPONED",
  "reason": "Too late to postpone"
}

### 13. Abandon a match that never started. Expects "match is not in progress".
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "MATCH_ABANDONED",
  "reason": "Crowd trouble outside the ground",
  "minute": 0
}

### 14. Unknown matchId. Expects "match not found".
POST {{host}}/matches/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "MATCH_STARTED"
}

### 15. Unknown discriminator. Expects Jackson to reject the subtype.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "NOT_A_REAL_EVENT"
}

### 16. Missing discriminator. Expects Jackson to reject the missing type id.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "no type field"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### IN-PLAY COMMANDS: all handled. Each needs the match IN_PROGRESS, so run
### block 1 first. Scoring and cards also need the players to be on the pitch.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 17. Goal scored.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "GOAL_SCORED",
  "clubId": "{{esperance}}",
  "playerId": "{{boualia}}",
  "minute": 48
}

### 18. Own goal.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "OWN_GOAL",
  "clubId": "{{sfaxien}}",
  "playerId": "{{omarBenAli}}",
  "minute": 31
}

### 19. Goal canceled. clubId is the club the cancelled goal was credited to,
### so for an own goal it is the conceding club's opponent.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "GOAL_CANCELED",
  "clubId": "{{esperance}}",
  "minute": 24
}

### 20. Yellow card.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "YELLOW_CARD_GIVEN",
  "clubId": "{{esperance}}",
  "playerId": "{{meriah}}",
  "minute": 38
}

### 21. Second yellow for the same player as block 20. There is no
### SECOND_YELLOW_CARD command: send YELLOW_CARD_GIVEN again and the aggregate
### emits SECOND_YELLOW_CARD plus RED_CARD_GIVEN itself.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "YELLOW_CARD_GIVEN",
  "clubId": "{{esperance}}",
  "playerId": "{{meriah}}",
  "minute": 71
}

### 22. Straight red.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "RED_CARD_GIVEN",
  "clubId": "{{sfaxien}}",
  "playerId": "{{maaloul}}",
  "minute": 74
}

### 23. Substitution. Rafia off, Msakni on.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "SUBSTITUTION",
  "clubId": "{{esperance}}",
  "playerOutId": "{{rafia}}",
  "playerInId": "{{msakni}}",
  "minute": 60
}

### 24. Penalty awarded.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "PENALTY_AWARDED",
  "clubId": "{{esperance}}",
  "minute": 78
}

### 25. Penalty scored.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "PENALTY_SCORED",
  "clubId": "{{esperance}}",
  "playerId": "{{msakni}}",
  "minute": 79
}

### 26. Penalty missed.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "PENALTY_MISSED",
  "clubId": "{{sfaxien}}",
  "playerId": "{{belwafi}}",
  "minute": 85
}

### 27. VAR check started. Opens a check; only one may be open at a time.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "VAR_CHECK_STARTED",
  "reason": "Possible penalty",
  "minute": 77
}

### 28. VAR decision. Closes the check opened in block 27. The decision is
### recorded as free text only: it emits no corrective event of its own, so
### cancelling a goal or awarding a penalty is a separate command.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "VAR_DECISION",
  "decision": "PENALTY_CONFIRMED",
  "minute": 78
}

### 29. Added time announced.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "ADDED_TIME_ANNOUNCED",
  "addedMinutes": 5
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### VALIDATION: @NotNull / @Min(0) / @NotBlank on the command records
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 30. Negative minute. Expects 400 from @Min(0).
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "GOAL_SCORED",
  "clubId": "{{esperance}}",
  "playerId": "{{boualia}}",
  "minute": -1
}

### 31. Missing required clubId/playerId. Expects 400 from @NotNull.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "GOAL_SCORED",
  "minute": 12
}

### 32. Blank VAR decision. Expects 400 from @NotBlank.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "VAR_DECISION",
  "decision": "",
  "minute": 78
}

### 33. Blank VAR check reason. Expects 400 from @NotBlank.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "VAR_CHECK_STARTED",
  "reason": "",
  "minute": 77
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### VAR GUARD RAILS: an open check must be decided before play moves on
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 34. Decision with no check open. Expects "no var check is awaiting a decision".
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "VAR_DECISION",
  "decision": "NO_OFFENCE",
  "minute": 78
}

### 35. Second check while one is open. Run block 27 first.
### Expects "a var check is awaiting a decision".
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "VAR_CHECK_STARTED",
  "reason": "Possible offside",
  "minute": 78
}

### 36. Half-time whistle with a check still open. Run block 27 first.
### Expects "a var check is awaiting a decision". FULL_TIME and
### SECOND_HALF_STARTED are blocked the same way.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "FIRST_HALF_ENDED"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### PLAYER IDENTITY: unknown players and players from the wrong club.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 37. Goal scored by a playerId that exists in no players row.
### Expects 404 PLAYER_NOT_FOUND.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "GOAL_SCORED",
  "clubId": "{{esperance}}",
  "playerId": "{{ghostPlayer}}",
  "minute": 50
}

### 38. Yellow card for a player that does not exist.
### Expects 404 PLAYER_NOT_FOUND, so no booking is recorded against a player
### nobody can look up.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "YELLOW_CARD_GIVEN",
  "clubId": "{{sfaxien}}",
  "playerId": "{{ghostPlayer}}",
  "minute": 52
}

### 39. Substitution bringing on a player that does not exist.
### Expects 404 PLAYER_NOT_FOUND, so no substitution slot is burned.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "SUBSTITUTION",
  "clubId": "{{esperance}}",
  "playerOutId": "{{belaili}}",
  "playerInId": "{{ghostPlayer}}",
  "minute": 55
}

### 40. Real player, wrong club: Maaloul plays for Sfaxien but the goal is
### credited to Esperance. Expects 400 PLAYER_NOT_IN_CLUB.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "GOAL_SCORED",
  "clubId": "{{esperance}}",
  "playerId": "{{maaloul}}",
  "minute": 57
}

### 41. Real player, wrong club: Boualia plays for Esperance but is sent off
### as a Sfaxien player. Expects 400 PLAYER_NOT_IN_CLUB.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "RED_CARD_GIVEN",
  "clubId": "{{sfaxien}}",
  "playerId": "{{boualia}}",
  "minute": 59
}

### 42. Substitution mixing clubs: Onana (Sfaxien) comes on for Rafia
### (Esperance) under Esperance's clubId. Expects 400 PLAYER_NOT_IN_CLUB,
### naming Onana. Both playerOutId and playerInId are checked.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "SUBSTITUTION",
  "clubId": "{{esperance}}",
  "playerOutId": "{{rafia}}",
  "playerInId": "{{onana}}",
  "minute": 61
}

### 43. clubId that is in no clubs row. Expects 404 CLUB_NOT_FOUND: the club
### check runs before the player check.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "GOAL_SCORED",
  "clubId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "playerId": "{{boualia}}",
  "minute": 63
}

### 44. Goal cancelled against a club that does not exist. Expects 404
### CLUB_NOT_FOUND. GOAL_CANCELED names no player, so this is the only check.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "GOAL_CANCELED",
  "clubId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "minute": 24
}

### 45. Penalty awarded to a club that does not exist. Expects 404
### CLUB_NOT_FOUND.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "PENALTY_AWARDED",
  "clubId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "minute": 78
}

### 46. Real club that is not in this match. Both clubs exist, so the service
### check passes and MatchAggregate.requireParticipant rejects it.
### Expects 400 CLUB_NOT_IN_MATCH. Needs a third club in the clubs table.
POST {{host}}/matches/{{matchId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "PENALTY_AWARDED",
  "clubId": "{{thirdClub}}",
  "minute": 80
}
